#: ../../../tests.rst:2
msgid "Testing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tests.rst:4
msgid ""
"Before contributing to Read the Docs, make sure your patch passes our test "
"suite and your code style passes our code linting suite."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tests.rst:7
msgid ""
"Read the Docs uses `Tox`_ to execute testing and linting procedures. Tox is "
"the only dependency you need to run linting or our test suite, the remainder "
"of our requirements will be installed by Tox into environment specific "
"virtualenv paths. Before testing, make sure you have Tox installed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tests.rst:15
msgid "pip install tox"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tests.rst:17
msgid "Running tests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tests.rst:19
msgid ""
"The test suite is split into separate tox environments that match the CI "
"pipeline:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tests.rst:27
msgid ""
"tox -e py312          # Core tests (no search, no proxito)\n"
"tox -e search         # Search tests (requires Elasticsearch)\n"
"tox -e proxito        # Proxito tests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tests.rst:28
msgid "To run all test suites at once:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tests.rst:33
msgid "tox -e py312,search,proxito"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tests.rst:34
msgid "To run a subset of tests:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tests.rst:39
msgid "tox -e py312 -- -k test_celery"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tests.rst:42
msgid ""
"Install ``tox-uv`` alongside tox for faster virtualenv creation and "
"dependency resolution:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tests.rst:50
msgid "Tox environments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tests.rst:52
msgid ""
"The ``tox`` configuration has the following environments configured. You can "
"target a single environment to limit the test suite:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tests.rst:55
msgid "py312"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tests.rst:56
msgid "Core tests — excludes search, proxito, and embed API markers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tests.rst:58
msgid "search"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tests.rst:59
msgid "Search tests — requires an Elasticsearch instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tests.rst:61
msgid "proxito"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tests.rst:62
msgid "Proxito tests — uses ``readthedocs.settings.proxito.test``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tests.rst:64
msgid "pre-commit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tests.rst:65
msgid "Run linting and formatting checks via pre-commit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tests.rst:67
msgid "migrations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tests.rst:68
msgid "Check for missing Django migrations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tests.rst:70
msgid "docs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tests.rst:71
msgid "Build user documentation with Sphinx."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tests.rst:73
msgid "docs-dev"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tests.rst:74
msgid "Build developer documentation with Sphinx."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tests.rst:80
msgid "Debug logging"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tests.rst:82
msgid ""
"Test failure reports only include ``WARNING`` and above log records, so the "
"error you're looking at isn't buried under ``DEBUG``/``INFO`` output from "
"the ``readthedocs`` logger."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tests.rst:86
msgid ""
"Full ``DEBUG`` output is always written to ``logs/debug.log`` by the "
"``debug`` file handler configured in ``readthedocs/settings/base.py``. After "
"a failing run, tail or open that file to see everything the failing test "
"logged — no re-running with extra flags required:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tests.rst:94
msgid "tail -n 200 logs/debug.log"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tests.rst:95
msgid ""
"If you'd rather see the debug records inline with the failure report, "
"override the level on the command line:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tests.rst:101
msgid "tox -e py312 -- --log-level=DEBUG -k test_something"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tests.rst:102
msgid "The ``WARNING`` threshold for the test report is set in two places:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tests.rst:104
msgid ""
"``pytest.ini`` — ``log_level = WARNING`` controls what pytest captures and "
"shows on test failure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tests.rst:106
msgid ""
"``readthedocs/settings/test.py`` — the Django ``console`` log handler is "
"pinned to ``WARNING`` for the test settings module."
msgstr ""

